{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>Were it not for the Elohim of my father, etc.</b> The reason he did not suffice to say ״the Elohim of my father, the Elohim of Abraham״ is that he intended to express two ideas: first, that inasmuch as He is the Elohim of my father, He stood by me and delivered me from your hand in my father's merit. Second, that He is the Master of ability, who oversees and judges with justice and saves the oppressed — and this is what he means by <b>the Elohim of Abraham</b>: meaning, the Elohim who publicized His divinity and truth to Abraham, and made His awesome deeds known in the world — that He is the Creator, He is the Bestower, and He judges with justice. And apart from this, if his father had another elohim, it would not have saved him from your hand, for there are many elohim that are of no avail to their worshippers — there is none like our Elohim, blessed be He." "<b>Further,</b> he may intend to say in this manner: <b>the Elohim of my father</b> corresponds to the merit of the fathers, and afterward he mentioned two attributes that he had which stood by him — namely, the attribute of Ḥesed and the attribute of Din. Corresponding to the attribute of Ḥesed he said <b>the Elohim of Abraham</b>, as it says (Micah 7:20) ״חֶסֶד לְאַבְרָהָם״, and corresponding to the attribute of Din he said <b>and the Pachad of Isaac.</b> Therefore he did not say ״the Elohim of Isaac,״ to allude to the attribute he intended; and apart from this he would have said ״the Elohim of Isaac,״ for we find that HaShem said to him (Genesis 28:13) ״אֱלֹהֵי יִצְחָק״. And the reason he mentioned these two attributes is to say that He showed extraordinary Ḥesed with him, and also executed judgment for him against Laban — these being the two attributes, and without one of them the good would not have reached Jacob." "<b>et my affliction, etc.</b> Meaning: had he not had the affliction, even though the truth was with him, HaShem would have been slow to anger and given him his reward in the supernal world; but on account of his affliction HaShem fulfilled for him (Deuteronomy 24:15) ״בְּיוֹמוֹ תִתֵּן שְׂכָרוֹ״ — and gave him the labor of his hands."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:27.419072252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}